{"id": "DeZdIDlIlTq", "title": "Video by shogentle", "description": "You don’t decide where people look. Contrast does.\n\nThe eye lands on the strongest contrast in the frame first, before the brain decides anything. Filmmakers have exploited that for a century. One red coat in a grey crowd. One warm face in a cold room. Orange against teal, which became a cliché for the boring reason that the two sit opposite each other on the color wheel, so they pop harder than any other pair.\n\nThe same rule runs everything in your frame. Text against the background. Your shirt against the wall. The subject against the set. Put any of them on a same-color background and the eye slides past, no matter how good the shot is. Pick one color to carry the eye and keep everything else quiet.\n\nTo start making cool videos, get my mini course. Comment MINI.\n\n#colortheory #videoediting #filmmaking #cinematicvideo #contentcreator", "channel": "shogentle", "uploader_id": "5965913552", "uploader": "AL, The Creator | Videography | Reels", "timestamp": 1791815617, "like_count": 4970, "comment_count": 211, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-2543113756186083a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 57.923, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fdmm2-4.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQOqQXVKaec3wZocm8PyyVib28go7zJwti5j2nszmDXr7V16VMHCv8Jxoa1MxFhZ35OYqrGwFjJblXRxZZY-pckHoJUKCxTEZqbpNLg.mp4?_nc_cat=108&_nc_oc=AdpxTDzUO-QfjFZYDtxOjgWZytKRXHv4gNnFJeRWE-ge2J8JbjRTmE8YyOa39TeYkQKxZazRGEouIGpTMmlItQNI&_nc_sid=9ca052&_nc_ht=instagram.fdmm2-4.fna.fbcdn.net&_nc_ohc=QVDLam2J2IoQ7kNvwEwJpLY&%3D%3D&ccb=17-1&_nc_gid=AViN_NbV8hk8lVPoV6mAVw&_nc_ss=7b689&_nc_zt=28&oh=00_AQRL8xZHK76nGfZm1AubAildqRtR2xF-fhWDbZGLgwY0Vg&oe=6AEFB6C5", "manifest_stream_number": 0, "is_dash_periods": true, "protocol": "https", "audio_ext": "m4a", "video_ext": "none", "vbr": 0, "abr": 57.923, "resolut